    "title": "Spain's Strangest Borders 🇪🇸🤯 An Island That Changes Country Every 6 Months!",
    "description": "Spain 🇪🇸 has some of the strangest borders in the world! Llívia is a Spanish town completely surrounded by France 🇫🇷, thanks to a technicality in the 1659 Treaty of the Pyrenees: it was a 'town', not a 'village' 😅 Pheasant Island belongs to Spain for six months and to France for the other six 🏝️ In Africa, Spain holds Ceuta and Melilla, the EU's only land borders with Africa, and Peñón de Vélez de la Gomera, whose 85 m border with Morocco 🇲🇦 is the world's shortest 🤯",
